tess (cust-success): Customer wants a minimal repro they can run in their staging with exact commands. They also want a short-term workaround they can ship this afternoon.

marco (eng-runtime): Minimal repro (server + slow client) — Node and curl variants below. These should trigger the behavior in ~10s on a moderate machine.

Server (express example):
```
const express=require('express');
const app=express();
app.get('/sse', (req,res)=>{
  res.setHeader('Content-Type','text/event-stream');
  res.setHeader('Cache-Control','no-cache');
  res.flushHeaders();
  let i=0;
  const t=setInterval(()=>{
    const ok=res.write(`data: ${i}\n\n`);
    if(!ok){
      console.warn('backpressure at',i);
      // stop writing for a tick to let socket drain
    }
    i++;
    if(i>2000) clearInterval(t);
  },1); // high produce rate
});
app.listen(8080);
```

Slow client via curl (simulate slow consumer):
```
curl -N http://localhost:8080/sse | pv -qL 10 > /dev/null
```
(pv rate-limits output to 10 bytes/sec)

Workaround for this afternoon:
- Turn off buffering on nginx: `proxy_buffering off; proxy_request_buffering off;`
- Increase ALB idle timeout to 300s (or > expected background pause)
- Add a short client-side keepalive that reads and discards frequent small pings so socket doesn't stall
- Use idempotency header `x-stream-session-id` so reconnects don't double-bill while we fix token expiry

alan (support): I'll send the repro and the quick workaround steps to the customer. We should also offer a playbook entry for Dedicated customers with nginx/ALB patterns.

sasha (sre): Action items:
- eng-runtime (marco) to add defensive drop/trim policy in streaming loop and a telemetry counter for `stream_backpressure_drops` (owner: marco, ETA: 1 week)
- ops to publish kernel-tuning doc for Dedicated (owner: sasha, ETA: 3 days)
- support (alan) to advise customer to disable proxy buffering and increase ALB idle timeout (owner: alan, today)
- product to consider server-side idempotency for streaming start events to prevent duplicate billing (cc @product)

marco (eng-runtime): one more note about billing: if a client reconnects and rewinds the prompt, we currently charge for the retried tokens. short-term we can detect immediate reconnects with same session id and mark them non-billable until stream resumes, but longer term product needs explicit idempotency semantics.

tess (cust-success): thanks everyone. customer confirmed they can toggle `proxy_buffering off` in staging and will run the repro. I'll update the thread with results. :thumbsup:

alan (support): ping me the staging logs once they run it, and include `strace -e write` or tcpdump if they can collect it.

